  accept 596                          -- Kin'weelay

# Stranglethorn's northern half at 36-37, between Desolace and Dustwallow (the 2026-11-07
# re-order; it came at 34-36, straight after Desolace and Hillsbrad, before).
#
# Flow: Shadowprey Village (where the previous guide ends) -> fly to Orgrimmar (Alliance
# Relations, training) -> zeppelin to Grom'gol (flight path) -> Nesingwary's camp -> young
# tigers and panthers and the Bloodscalp trolls -> the road south to Booty Bay (flight path,
# bind) -> fly to Grom'gol -> the river camp -> Nesingwary -> tigers and panthers ->
# Nesingwary -> elder tigers -> Nesingwary -> the basilisks, raptors and Bloodscalp village ->
# Nesingwary -> Booty Bay -> fly to Grom'gol -> Lashtail raptors -> the Vile Reef and the
# Bloodscalp ruins -> Grom'gol -> Shadowmaw, the tigresses and the Snapjaw river -> the
# Shadowmaw panthers -> the Venture Co. camp -> the Mosh'Ogg camp -> Grom'gol, where the next
# guide takes the zeppelin to Orgrimmar.
#
# Optional extras:
# - Crystal in the Mountains (635) starts from the Pendant of Myzrael, a 0.01-0.08% drop from
#   the trolls; take it only if one drops (it ends in Arathi).
# - The Green Hills of Stranglethorn (338-342): its pages drop at about 1% each from the
#   vale's trolls (or buy them). The chapters are accepted at Nesingwary's camp and turned in
#   later if you have them.
#
# Some Assembly Required (577) is accepted and its skins gathered here, and handed in on the
# Booty Bay stop of forever/horde/40-50/01-stranglethorn-vale.
#
# Class training: in Orgrimmar at the start (Druids in Thunder Bluff on the flight from
# Shadowprey; Paladins train next with Garen Largo in the Undercity, at about 38). The Warlock
# Felhunter's Damaged Chest stop (1803) is in forever/class/warlock/felhunter-horde.
#
# Carried on: Trollbane (638) for Arathi (forever/horde/30-40/05-arathi-highlands).
#
# Not taken: Marg Speaks (1261): Marg's note is offered only after The Troll Witchdoctor
# (1240), which is turned in at Grom'gol in forever/horde/40-50/01-stranglethorn-vale.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Nesingwary's camp

step Nesingwary's camp
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip Follow the road north out of Grom'gol; Nesingwary's hunting camp sits on the hill north-east of the river. From here on, keep every page of The Green Hills of Stranglethorn you loot: Barnil asks for them later.
  accept 583                          -- Barnil Stonepot
  turnin 583                          -- Hemet Nesingwary
  turnin 5762
  turnin 5763
  accept 194
  accept 185                          -- Ajeck Rouack
  accept 190                          -- Sir S. J. Erlgadin

step Nesingwary's Expedition: kill these as you meet them
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip Young Stranglethorn Tigers prowl west of the camp, Young Panthers south and east of it.
  tip Head west past the camp. Stranglethorn Raptors (33-34) hunt the clearings, and the Bloodscalp trolls hold the ruins on the coast: every Bloodscalp can drop a tusk. A Pendant of Myzrael is a very rare drop from them: if one drops, read it.
  tip Careful: The troll camps have many patrolling mobs, so other trolls often join a fight.
  kill 681 quest 185
  kill 683 quest 190
  collect 3901 quest 581
  collect 4614 x1 optional
  accept 635 optional

step Booty Bay
  tip Follow the road south to Booty Bay at the southern tip of the vale and enter through the tunnel in the cliffs. Stay on the road: the jungle beside it is well above your level. Gringer, the Horde flight master, waits on the upper deck.
  accept 575                          -- Drizzlik, inside
  vendor nearest
  accept 605                          -- Crank Fizzlebub, inside
  accept 213                          -- Kebok, upstairs
  getfp "Booty Bay" npc 2858          -- Gringer
  accept 189                          -- Kebok
  accept 201                          -- Krazek, upstairs
  sethome "Booty Bay"                 -- Upstairs

